[Music]  for those of you who are wondering what  happened to the next heroes path  no worries it's still coming i  definitely plan to tie up this series in  a neat little bow however  now that the second presentation of  hyrule warriors has come and gone there  is a little less pressure to release the  last two episodes at the same speed i  did with the previous ones  we have until the end of november until  the game releases after all  episode 6 is scheduled to go up this  weekend and 7 will follow the week after  so i hope you look forward to that  in the meantime since we have a new  trailer now i thought i'd do what every  self-respecting zelda obsessed gaming  nerd does and  overanalyze stuff that most people  probably glossed over and wouldn't  even be bothered by it to begin with  today i want to talk about this specific  clip from the trailer  which is my favorite one with the  opening shot of akala citadel as a close  second  despite being only one and a half  seconds long this shot was probably a  big eye-catcher  for a lot of people as someone who has  been researching and obsessing over the  great calamity for the past weeks  this little piece of footage was just  pure eye candy  finally being able to see the immense  scale and chaos that went on in central  hyrule is  amazing also sad for the inhabitants  but amazing for me there are a couple of  things i want to go over in regards to  this shot so  let's start with some of the smaller  ones first off we finally have an idea  of just how many guardians were roaming  around central hyrule that night and  well safe to say there were a lot of  them second  aside from guardian stalkers which have  always been depicted as the main  antagonist during the invasion we can  clearly see a significant amount of  skywatches flying around as well proving  that they were just as much a part of  the forces that eradicated the  settlements garrisons and other  important landmarks across hyrule  in breath of the wild none of the  cutscenes from the calamity showed the  sky watchers in action and instead  only showed the stalkers doing the dirty  work we did see them briefly in the  first trailer for age of calamity but  only at castletown  it makes sense that they too played a  big part in the invasion since we can  still find some of them roaming around  in various locations in breath of the  wild most notably at akala citadel  so it's nice to finally see this  confirmed in an actual cutscene  another thing to note is that the  destruction of central hyrule took place  at night and in rainy weather which  matches perfectly with the cutscenes of  lincoln zelda during the event  specifically the one where zelda breaks  down and the one where link and zelda  are at fort hatteno  just the fact that they managed to match  the weather conditions and the time of  day is very promising  by the way i want to quickly mention  this as i feel it's important  some people seem to assume that the  calamity itself spanned across multiple  days and some even suggesting weeks  and that linc and zelda might have had  to camp out at specific moments or  something like that  but i can assure you that this is not  the case the calamity only lasted about  12 hours tops  it starts at sundown when zelda returns  from the spring then the main invasion  and eradication of hyrule takes place  mostly at night which is also when zelda  awakens her power  then by the time zelda arrives at the  great forest to return the master sword  knight has turned to day  and then she continues to seal away  ganon of course the castle is covered in  dark clouds so it doesn't look like  midday in the scene  the calamity was a swift and merciless  defeat it's why there are so few  survivors the hylians were caught  completely off guard and barely had time  to evacuate anyone  besides do you really think that zelda  and link were able to camp out amidst  all of this i don't think so and if  you're still on the fence about this  both breath of the wild and creating a  champion refer to the event as the day  of the great calamity at multiple  occasions  anyway from this fact we can also derive  that this shot from the age of calamity  trailer takes place  around the same time as the scene where  zelda breaks down however still  slightly before it since zelda mentions  during the cutscene that the champions  are now  quote trapped inside those things but as  we can see here vana boris has not yet  been taken over and still maintains its  original blue glow  speaking of vana boris it's time for the  main event  aside from the sheer amount of guardians  blasting their way through central  hyrule the second thing that catches the  attention is that it's basically being  observed from her bosa's point of view  atop her divine beast  which brings up an important question  where exactly is vana boris located at  this point  and which part of central hyrule is she  observing what are we looking at here  i think most of us kind of assumed that  the divine beasts were roughly in the  same location as the firing positions we  saw in breath of the wild at the moment  they were taken over  which in vanna boris case is on  spectacle rock but as we can see in the  trailer spectacle rock is right here  with the wasteland tower right next to  it  so apparently vana boris was nowhere  near spectacle rock at that moment  so where is she the way the shot is lit  gives us very little to work with  as most of it is too dark to see any  definitive landmarks in central hyrule  turning up the brightness or the  contrast doesn't do much  there simply isn't enough pixel  information to work with  everything still just blends together so  the only thing we really have as a  reference is the skyline in the  background  now this is what i believe to be roughly  where the shot was taken from  which in the case of my shot here is  atop the shika tower located in central  hyrule  and herbosa as well as our divine beast  are looking in this general direction  we have the great plateau here and  spectacle rock here as a reference  that is pretty damn crazy since just  look at how close to hyrule castle that  actually is  but before we get into what this means  for the story let's first look at how i  came to this conclusion  because when we look at my shot and the  one from the trailer side by side we can  see that there are definitely some  significant differences  and this has to do with a number of  factors as mentioned before the horizon  is the main anchor point here  by matching up the alignment of various  shapes and structures we can get a  pretty accurate estimation of where  naboris is located on the x and y axis  on the map but as mentioned before there  are some significant differences between  the two compositions  first off in my shot we can see a lot  more of the horizon than in the trailer  if we were to crop out the part of the  skyline we see in the trailer it would  look something like this  so does this mean we are too far away  not necessarily  notice how this crossroad here is  visible in the trailer  yet in the cropped out version it falls  off screen the best explanation for this  difference is the type of camera being  used in the trailer compared to the one  in my composition  and in particular the focal length of  the camera for those who are unfamiliar  with how focal length works  it basically determines how wide or  narrow the field of view of the camera  is the longer the focal length the  narrower the field of view and vice  versa  some cameras have a dynamic field of  view while others have a static one and  can only change their field of view by  changing the lens  by adjusting the focal length of a  camera while simultaneously changing the  distance to an object you can actually  zoom in on the background while the  foreground object stays the same size  there are various reasons for using  either a long or short focal length  gopros for instance always have a very  wide angle lens  since you want to capture as much of the  environment as possible  something that's also interesting to  note is that the wider the lens becomes  the more the image gets distorted and  you get this spherical look as if you  can see the curvature of the earth on  the horizon  which of course in real life isn't  observable that's why the earth is flat  you can even see this slight warped  effect in my capture  of course i don't have any control over  the focal length of the camera in breath  of the wild but i made a little  demonstration of what this would look  like  all i'm doing here is changing the y  position of the camera while  simultaneously changing the focal length  of the camera  notice how we can see more and then less  of hyrule field but mount hylia stays  the same size  this wouldn't happen if i don't adjust  the focal length in this case the  mountains get smaller and bigger while  the camera moves back and forth  long story short the camera in the  trailer shot is likely using a different  focal length than the one in breath of  the wild  hence why the compositions are not  identical because of this it's  impossible to pinpoint the location of  vano boris with 100  accuracy but we can get pretty close i'm  fairly certain that in terms of the  x-axis and the angle of view we are  definitely on  point as stated before this is mainly  due to the alignment of different  elements found on the horizon  if we take the skyline from the trailer  and put it against the one from my shot  and then adjust for the field of view we  can see that they are very close  again there are factors which make it  impossible to get a 100  match such as the aforementioned camera  type but also the elevation  we don't exactly know how high vana  boris is and even if we did  it's unlikely that the model scale from  the trailer is the exact same as the one  found in breath of the wild  it might not even be the exact same  model who knows  i am standing on the central shika tower  which i'm fairly sure  isn't the exact same height as fauna  boris we also have to take into account  that the shot in the trailer isn't right  behind the divine beast  it's not actually a pov shot from  herbosa's eyes the camera is positioned  slightly to the left  and away from her and i will never be  able to get the camera in that exact  same spot  but it's the alignments which really  matter here and by observing these  alignments we can make pretty accurate  guesses as to where  certain landmarks are this little peak  here for instance is unmistakably the  rooftop of the temple of time  this shape here is in fact two different  mountain tops  one close and one much further away from  this alignment we can confirm that this  area right here  is the colosseum and this purple lit  strip is likely the bridge  leading to it this garrison or keep  right here matches with the ruin found  in front of the moat surrounding the  coliseum  the rock formation seen right above her  bosa seems to be  mount gustav etc and this is why i think  the angle of view and the exposition of  noboras is pretty accurate  if we even slightly move to either the  right or left of the position we're  currently at  the alignments completely fall apart  especially the mountain peaks as well as  the temple of time no longer match up at  all  when it comes to the actual field below  there are still some significant  differences  however i think most of that can be  chalked up to either some of the reasons  i mentioned before  or alterations done to the map of age of  calamity there seems to be a lot more  rock formations on the ground but  hyrule's geography could have changed in  between games  some rocks may have been blasted away or  eroded or  you know maybe even stomped into the  ground by ivana boris waltzing around  centro hyrule  which brings me to the final segment  with this rough estimate of the location  of vana boris in the trailer  what does this mean for the story well  aside from all the ruins in central  hyrule there's also a huge amount of  dead guardians found around these parts  and vana boris may have had a large  stake in this it might even hint at  and dare i say a playable section where  you are able to stomp smash  zap and electrocute guardians around  central hyrule which would of course be  absolutely amazing but let's not get our  hopes up too much  still the fact that urbosa managed to  get vanaborus onto the fields of central  hyrule all the way from gerudo desert  is pretty damn awesome and now that i  think about it the artwork shown at the  end of both trailers  actually shows vanna boris walking  around central hyrule in the background  very close to the castle we don't see  any other divine beasts in this artwork  either  so it might be that herbosa was the only  one to gather divine beasts this close  to ganon before it was finally corrupted  and taken over  i mean out of all champions urbosa has  by far the biggest grudge against ganon  due to the history which tells that  calamity ganon once took on the form of  a gerudo and just in case you were  wondering i'm not using this new  information to update the hero's path  episode about urbosa  the reason being that the paths laid out  in those videos are based on what we  know from breath of the wild and  creating a champion  and make gameplay suggestions based on  that the whole goal of the series is to  see  how this will ultimately stack up  against the story events presented in  age of calamity  anyway that pretty much wraps it up for  this one this turned into a much longer  video than i originally had in mind but  hey when in rome get it all right bye  [Music]  you

